# 7. PREVENT REDIRECT CHAINS AND LOOPS

Build a reliable redirect policy.

Requirements:

- Every legacy URL should redirect directly to the final active destination where possible.
- Do not redirect from legacy URL A to legacy URL B if B then redirects to active URL C.
- Validate destination slugs against the current active catalog.
- Avoid self-redirects.
- Avoid redirecting a fallback destination back to the original URL.
- Do not generate a new redirect on every request using an unstable slug transformation.
- Make resolution deterministic for the same catalog state and input.
- Keep the active catalog as the authority for destination validity.

If an old URL maps to an active slug that later changes, the resolver must be able to follow the latest active destination without creating a redirect loop.

Where a legacy mapping table already exists, integrate it rather than creating conflicting rules.

